MIME — Face Is Not All You Need: MIME Benchmark for Incomplete Multimodal Emotion Recognition
Proceedings of the 34th ACM International Conference on Multimedia (ACM MM '26)
DOI: 10.1145/3767308.3838643
Project page: https://yuxinokk.github.io/MIME/

This repository contains two kinds of material, released under different terms.

1. Code
-------
All source code in this repository (in particular everything under `eval/`) is
released under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
(CC BY 4.0).

You are free to share and adapt the code for any purpose, including
commercially, provided that you give appropriate credit, link to the license,
and indicate if changes were made.

Full license text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
Human-readable summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

2. Benchmark data
-----------------
The MIME benchmark data (video segments, annotations, Chain-of-Emotion
reasoning chains) is released for ACADEMIC AND NON-COMMERCIAL RESEARCH USE
ONLY.

- The sample set distributed in this repository (4 clips per subset, 28 clips
  in total, plus `label.jsonl`) may be used for research and evaluation, and
  may be redistributed unmodified together with this notice.
- Access to the full 2,000-segment benchmark requires a signed copy of
  `license.pdf`. Requests should be sent to jinj62062@gmail.com, CC
  lanx@cse.neu.edu.cn.
- Redistribution, resale, or any commercial use of the full benchmark data is
  not permitted without written permission from the authors.

The source videos are derived from CAER, DFEW, MAFW, FERV39k and publicly
available social media videos. Users are responsible for complying with the
original terms of those source datasets.

